Notebook[{
Cell["Hypermatrix", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"f3a9fa84-ab30-0d48-899a-90361dc23c4c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f179dbff-9cea-2146-a0aa-066fbec87a99"],
 " ",
 "represents the given arrays as a hypermatrix, holding them in canonical \
order."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"df8531c5-befd-1743-aeef-b4f83cd37a2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b44ea25c-3717-934d-907a-e9e46f5516d8"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"500021bf-c6ae-2e4a-8c18-15d4eba63a45"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"b121ad07-d2bc-304e-aef1-08a021dca35e"],

Cell["\<\
The arrays are ordered by array order, lowest first; then by dimensions, \
shorter first, compared term by term; then by symmetry, taking \"Symmetric\" \
before \"Cyclic\" before \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f9c14f1d-fe3f-df4a-b979-725c220cc6f3"],

Cell["\<\
Two arrays alike in all three are put in the Wolfram Language's own canonical \
order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the set of arrays it was given \
and of nothing else. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"624d5da9-58cb-cf46-8ba7-0428dca93b64"],

Cell["\<\
An irregular array is necessarily \"Rigid\", since only a regular array can \
carry a symmetry, so the symmetry criterion separates the regular arrays \
among themselves.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7d2993aa-cdc8-5844-a98b-32d82112002d"],

Cell["\<\
Arrays of any kind of entry sit together freely. Raw entries given in place \
of an array are promoted to an ArrayObject.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"99e91494-5e51-6742-9654-458f0030d801"],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, and Normal the entries of each of them in \
order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3188cb2d-9046-2e45-87b5-846b81ade01d"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"02af56d6-9fab-8d49-aceb-e57631eaaada"],

Cell["The arrays are sorted whatever order they are given in:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"1c4e563e-1faf-3d4e-b776-968234f7fc5a"],

Cell["\<\
hm = Hypermatrix[{
   ArrayObject[Array[1 &, {2, 2, 2}], \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2, 3}],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Cyclic\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b6fd74c7-22ef-ee43-a5a7-8d4758529297"],

